merge("entities/european-parliament.md", u"""
## The 2024 elections

The [[2024-european-parliament-elections|June 2024 elections]] to the 720-seat assembly returned a clear centrist majority of more than 400 seats while delivering significant gains to nationalist and anti-immigrant groups, projected at roughly 130 seats, a better showing than in 2019, with conservatives marking a decisive victory.[{N}] Badlands commentary characterized the body as globalist-centered and argued that because the European Union is far from a sovereign actor on the world stage, a parliamentary majority matters mainly for EU policy and trade among member states, which is why the twice-a-decade elections normally see low turnout and enthusiasm.[{N}] The 2024 round broke that pattern with record turnout, which the commentary read as a bellwether of continental sentiment swinging toward strong borders and anti-interventionism rather than as a direct change in national leadership.[{N}]
""")

