merge("concepts/texas-deceptive-trade-practices-act.md", u"""
## Use in the 2024 vehicle data investigation

In June 2024 Attorney General [[ken-paxton|Ken Paxton]] invoked the Act to open an investigation into several car manufacturers reported to be collecting large volumes of driver data directly from vehicles and selling it to third parties, including insurers.[{N}] The statute authorizes the Office of the Attorney General to investigate false, misleading, or deceptive acts or practices, and on that basis manufacturers and the third-party purchasers were instructed to produce documents about their conduct and about the disclosures they made to customers regarding data collection and sale.[{N}]
""")
